{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Closing verification (sanctioned non-force path), main @9bdb22f5887. Ticked 5 of 7 ACs; TWO left deliberately unticked.\n\nTICKED:\n- AC1 (primitive): batch_stage_and_commit at src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:479 — one lock, M UUID-named event files, one 'git add' + one commit. Pinned by tests/unit/test_store_batch_write.py::test_batch_commits_all_events_in_a_single_commit.\n- AC2 (importer chunked; single-event path unchanged): src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:190-196 routes through it in _CHUNK (256) sized chunks; only the importer sets the _seam.batch_sink contextvar (src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:35-51). Pinned by tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batching.py::test_interactive_writes_stay_one_commit_per_event.\n- AC3 (atomicity + crash-resume; union-merge/compaction regressions): atomicity — test_validation_failure_rolls_back_before_any_commit, test_commit_failure_rolls_back_whole_batch_and_next_write_is_clean, test_malformed_event_mid_chunk_rolls_back_whole_chunk. Crash-resume idempotence — test_crash_before_later_chunk_leaves_whole_commit_or_none_and_resumes (source_id re-scan skips committed chunks). Union-merge/compaction: the mechanism-level guarantee is that each event keeps its own byte-identical file, pinned by test_batch_bytes_are_canonical_and_identical_to_single_path; since union-merge and SNAPSHOT compaction key off event UUIDs and not commit boundaries, they cannot observe a difference.\n- AC6 (cross-clone convergence + compaction unaffected): same byte-identity argument plus test_batched_import_equivalent_to_per_event / test_batched_import_full_wireup_equivalent (batched import replays to the SAME logical state as a per-event import) and test_batch_self_heals_preexisting_unmerged_bridge_state.\n- AC7 (single-event write path unchanged): test_interactive_writes_stay_one_commit_per_event + test_batch_bytes_are_canonical_and_identical_to_single_path.\n\nVerified now: '.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_store_batch_write.py tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batching.py tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py -q' -> 14 passed (151s).\n\nLEFT UNTICKED (genuinely not delivered as written):\n- AC4 'benchmark: large-import wall-clock before vs after' — the benchmark that shipped measures COMMIT COUNT, not wall-clock: tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass asserts a synthetic N=3000 import makes exactly 2*ceil(3000/256) commits, a >=10x reduction vs the ~2N per-event baseline. No before/after wall-clock measurement exists.\n- AC5 'completes in a fraction of the per-event wall-clock, with the same resulting logical state' — the second half IS proven (test_batched_import_equivalent_to_per_event), but the wall-clock half is not measured anywhere.\n\nThese two need an operator decision: either run and record the wall-clock benchmark, or amend the ACs to the commit-count proxy that was actually chosen (and re-run review-plan). Note also that the broader op-batching-for-all-mutations work remains tracked by the still-open e3d0-16d9-61ca-4862, which this ticket already links as a duplicate."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786087125216285001,"uuid":"0016f4dd-8eb1-4454-a010-c54a6943137d"}